<title>USA: Bankers Trust says 22 firms selling its funds.</title>
<headline>Bankers Trust says 22 firms selling its funds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankers Trust New York Corp said on Wednesday that 22 new financial institutions are now selling funds managed by the firm's Global Investment Management unit through no-transaction fee arrangements, or wrap accounts since the beginning of the year.</p>
<p>This has increased its mutual fund family assets in the United States by 30 percent since the start of the year to $15 billion, Bankers Trust said.</p>
<p>Bankers Trust manages more than $230 billion in assets worldwide, it said.</p>
